      "groups": [
        {
          "id": "cet4-paper-2015122-part-3-section-1-group-1",
          "title": "Question 26 to 35 are based on the following passage.",
          "presentation": "reading",
          "instructions": [],
          "stimulusBlocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "runs": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Scholars of the information society are divided over whether social inequality decreases or increases in an information-based society. However, they generally agree with the idea that inequality in the information society is "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015122-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-26"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " different from that of an industrial society. As information progresses in society, the cause and structural nature of social inequality changes as well. It seems that the information society "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015122-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-27"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " the quantity of information available to the members of a society by revolutionizing the ways of using and exchanging information. But such a view is a "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015122-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-28"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " analysis based on the quantity of information supplied by various forms of the mass media. A different "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015122-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-29"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " is possible when the actual amount of information "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015122-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-30"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " by the user is taken into account. In fact, the more information "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015122-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-31"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " throughout the entire society, the wider the gap becomes between “information haves” and “information have-nots”, leading to digital divide. According to recent studies, digital divide has been caused by three major "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015122-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-32"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " : class, sex, and generation. In terms of class, digital divide exists among different types of workers and between the upper and middle classes and the lower class. With "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015122-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-33"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " to sex, digital divide exists between men and women. The greatest gap, however, is between the Net-generation, "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015122-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-34"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " with personal computers and the Internet, and the older generation, "
                },
                {
                  "type": "blank",
                  "blankId": "cet4-paper-2015122-part-3-section-1-group-1-blank-35"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " to an industrial society."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
